Z||000000||maryjane||11-09-2001||12:15 AM||||Is it just another day where you live??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||11-09-2001||12:24 AM||||Not hardly.  No matter where I am or what I'm doing on Veteran's Day, I take a silent moment to thank those who've gone before to create and protect this great country of ours.  And I did that before Sept. 11th.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>To our veterans - <I><B>Thank You.</B></I>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Cooter||11-09-2001||12:28 AM||||Around here, people can't even decide when Veterans' Day is. We are out of school tomorrow, while some are out Monday and others are not even able to have the day off. It is sad that the people who should be our heros are silently passing away without the recognition they deserve. We owe so much of what we have to the people who fought and died for our freedom- yet many people just see it as a day off work. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||11-09-2001||12:37 AM||||Nope... Not just another day... Lots of people gave up everything for us to be as we are today. You can't refute that, even if you are a tree-hugging hippie-crite. I pay my respects.<P>Unfortunately I'm working this year, but I usually attend the ceremonies if I can get away with it... I do buy my Poppies, though.||||reg||7
Z||000004||California Kid||11-09-2001||12:40 AM||||Pretty much a tough day for me, lost to many friends in Vietnam, only to return to the U.S. and be protested against upon arrival.<P>While there are scattered events that take place locally here, the general public just doesn't understand the pains of war, what our soldiers have sacrificed, or given their lives for.||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||11-09-2001||12:53 AM||||I wasn't infering it was just another day, I've just noticed it isn't observed as visibly as July 4th, etc. To me, it's equally important. But then, I ALWAYS pay special attention to this upcoming weekend, for other reasons. So do several other PFF members. (to be explained in a day or two).<BR>Now, I don't mean to hijack my own thread, but came to my attention that during the Iran-Contra senate hearing, Oliver North was questioned about a $60,000 security system he installed at his private home. He explained that he needed it because he had been threatened by a foreign national. When pressed for a name, he gave it. One Ossama Bin Laden. Called him the most dangerous man in the world. He suggested that Bin Laden be assasinated....15 years ago.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||11-09-2001||12:59 AM||||Ok, NOW I'm confused  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>I can only guess that you've (and other members) have lost friends in the various scuffles that have occured in the past, say, 50 years? <p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||5
