Z||000008||Monkeyman||11-09-2001||01:47 AM||||Veterans Day is actually meant to pay tribute to anyone who has served in the military, not just those who fought in a war/conflict.  On the other hand, I don't think I contributed much while I was in the Army.  Not a whole lot I can do to pay tribute around here and a pilgrimage to Arlington is out of the question.<P>Looking forward to your surprise, maryjane.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Butter||11-09-2001||11:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Veterans Day is actually meant to pay tribute to anyone who has served in the military, not just those who fought in a war/conflict.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Thank You and I Do.<BR>I was more fortunate than those who, I pay tribute too, that sacrificed more than me.  I will also have in mind those brave men and women that have a job to do at the present.<P>I REMEMBER AND I THANK ALL.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000010||blazin'||11-09-2001||11:38 AM||||Rememberance day is important to me, I lost a great-grandfather in WW1, of course I never met him, but to imagine what it was like to fight in a war....It's unimaginable.<P>The school I attend, we have a ceremony for the vet's, and last year, during the moment of silence, people were laughing and talking their heads off! All the while, there were like five veterans in attendence. I can't imagine the feeling of disrespect they must have felt||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tonker||11-09-2001||06:39 PM||||I'm going to try to make my way downtown for the ceremony at the Cenotaph on Sun. BTW Are poppies worn in the US?||||reg||5
